# Four cells on paper in one row, 64px pitch. Each cell holds a container moved with `at:` to the cell's center, and every child inside has no `at:`, so each mark must sit centered in its own cell. A mark off center, or missing, is a failure.
# 1. `group at:32,32` holding a gold circle (radius 14): a gold disc centered in the first cell.
# 2. `layer at:96,32` holding a blue 28x28 square: a blue square centered in the second cell.
# 3. `group at:160,32` with a `mask` of a 24x24 rect and a red circle (radius 20): the mask cuts the circle to a red 24x24 square centered in the third cell. An empty cell means the mask missed the circle.
# 4. `group at:224,32` holding `repeat 3 rot:60` of a green 4x44 rect: six green spokes, 60 degrees apart, crossing at the fourth cell's center like an asterisk.
@artboard 256x64
@target structure/group_origin.png

group at:32,32
  circle 14 fill:p.gold

layer moved at:96,32
  rect 28 fill:p.blue

group at:160,32
  mask
    rect 24 fill:p.paper
  circle 20 fill:p.red

group at:224,32
  repeat 3 rot:60
    rect 4x44 fill:p.green
